[!INFO]
Node 20 (April 2023) & Node 22 (April 2025)
shipped further hardening: several
child_process
helpers now copy user-supplied
options
with
CopyOptions()
instead of using them by reference.  This blocks pollution of nested objects such as
stdio
, but
does not protect against the
NODE_OPTIONS
/
--import
tricks
described above â those flags are still accepted via environment variables.
A full fix would have to restrict which CLI flags can be propagated from the parent process, which is being tracked in Node Issue #50559.
